#' Field description: observedDropoutProportion 2
#' @field observedDropoutProportion2 Mean replication-specific observed dropout proportion in arm 2, counting dropout before the event and by the arm or population's last contributing analysis. Only replications with a finite finishing horizon and positive enrolled-subject denominator contribute; NA if none contribute. Available only for patient-wise simulation. Numeric vector over scenarios for two-arm trials; in multi-arm trials, arm 1 is a matrix of active-arm rows and scenario columns (a vector for one active arm), and arm 2 is a vector over scenarios for shared control. In enrichment trials, both arms have population rows (subpopulations followed by the full population) and scenario columns, or a vector for one population. Discontinued arms and populations are retained; overlapping populations include their shared subjects. There is no stage dimension. NULL for test-statistic-based simulation.
#' @keywords internal
